join Syn_Lucretia rightmost
Syn_Lucretia: Alright, they’re gone. Now tell me why in the world you would agree to this “deal.”
join Lucretia leftmost
Lucretia: I didn’t have any other choice. I was trapped in my room and the zombies were killing everyone. I had no hope of fighting back… but I swear, I didn’t know he would do this to us.
Syn_Lucretia: “Us.” So it’s true then. We’re both Lucretia, right?
Lucretia: In exchange for the powers, he asked to take half of my soul back to his home realm. I didn’t realize the other half would still be conscious, but… yeah.
Syn_Lucretia: Home realm, huh? Yeah, that sounds about right. I can’t believe my other half would be so stupid.
Lucretia: Hey! Without these powers we’d both be dead. So you’re welcome.
Syn_Lucretia: No, we’re still good as dead! Having your mind split in two doesn’t seem real sustainable for daily functioning, if you ask me. And there’s no way I’m just staying here.
Lucretia: Well what could we even do? Where would you even go?
Syn_Lucretia: You find Argus, and get him to undo your stupid deal. And in the meantime, I’ll try to find a way back to your realm. Maybe go to that huge statue in the distance. That looks super ominous and important, right?
Lucretia: Alright. Fine. I don't know how the hell I’m supposed to convince an otherworldly entity to just “undo” everything, but we don’t really have any other choice. Let’s do this.